      "writtenOn": "2023-08-14T10:58:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a completely different thing which is in particular meant for backward compatibility. No flag \u003d no callback about local networks. Consider the following existing code in an old app :\n\n    cm.registerNetworkCallback(\n      new NetworkRequest.Builder().addTransport(WIFI).build(),\n      myCallback);\n\nThis old code is likely not actually ready to receive callbacks about local networks like a tethering downstream. So by default it doesn\u0027t see them.\n\nConversely, you can create a callback that will see all Wifi networks *including* the local agents, by setting this flag but not the capability.\n\nI added some doc, and a runtime check to help developers.",
      "parentUuid": "72875cd6_72b0a8a5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3893,
        "startChar": 32,
        "endLine": 3893,
        "endChar": 59
      },
      "revId": "7eba2f3968f4f640aefad980de66b7a4a33319f7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
